P port 8181 while SELinux remains in enforcing mode (confirmed via correct http_port_t SELinux port labeling for 8181, not by disabling MAC). Verified reachability, persistence across a full node restart, and no AVC denials.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1: CentOS Stream 10, SELinux enforcing (targeted policy), no httpd/inventory app present, port 8181 free\",\"Installed httpd and policycoreutils-python-utils via dnf\",\"Created inventory app content at /var/www/inventory/index.html\",\"Configured /etc/httpd/conf.d/inventory.conf to Listen on 8181 and serve the inventory app as a VirtualHost\",\"Added SELinux port context: semanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181 (confirmed as local customization via semanage port -l -C), then restorecon on the docroot\",\"Enabled and started httpd; confirmed active/enabled, port 8181 listening, HTTP 200 response with correct content, SELinux still Enforcing, no AVC denials in kernel log or audit log\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, machine-id, SELinux mode, httpd status, HTTP 200 check\",\"Issued a self-acknowledging reboot (backgrounded systemctl reboot after ack) on node1\",\"Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned; confirmed changed boot_id proving an actual restart\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: SELinux Enforcing, httpd active+enabled, port 8181 listening, SELinux port context intact, HTTP 200 with correct inventory content\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Inventory app served over TCP 8181 on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5f68844d060e4a0a\",\"cmd-94fa93121a1947c4\",\"cmd-4ad9285e2810418a\"],\"summary\":\"Created inventory app + httpd vhost listening on 8181, started httpd, confirmed port listening and curl returned HTTP 200 with inventory content\"},{\"requirement\":\"SELinux remains enforcing while serving on non-standard port 8181 (MAC compliance, not bypass)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-59e0c10fa48b4fe4\",\"cmd-1415214c2726483c\",\"cmd-4c9465e1c7b14d39\",\"cmd-ee3aaf4c8262436d\",\"cmd-94f